			"description": "Lye Swing - painted big-band score after Len Lye (Swinging the Lambeth Walk, Free Radicals). Five shapes, one per sound band: Ring = low, Strokes = low-mid, Wave = mid, Cross = mid-high, Zigzag = high. Each shape measures its band against its own recent peaks, so every shape answers the music by itself. Scale sizes everything relative to the output height. Spectrum In: Composition or External. Sound: Sensitivity (how readily shapes appear), Fade (seconds to fall back), Show Meter (level bars and range readout). Physics: Boil (redraws the shapes 12 times per second, like paint on film), Punch (a short size push on the attack of a note). Backdrop: Backdrop On, Backdrop Color (off = transparent). Per shape: X, Y (-1..1 = frame edges), Size, Rotation, Count (0-8 copies in a row), Spacing, Scatter, Color, and one form control (Ring Fill, Strokes Thickness, Wave Height, Cross Arm Width, Zigzag Height). Automate position, size and rotation in Arena for movement.",
			"displayName": "Lye Swing",
